/* Black neoprene CubeOne test — the data behind the "real test" section on
   /rubber-testing. GENERATED from the 2026-08-21-CONTROL-BLACK NEOPRENE export
   (samples.csv, and each slot folder's stress_strain.csv and xmotor.csv);
   regenerate from the export rather than hand-editing numbers.

   - The run is 10 specimens. The export folder also holds slot 12 (the last test,
     2:43 PM), which is left out as agreed. Every statistic here is recomputed over
     slots 2–11, so it differs slightly from the export's summary.csv (which
     averages all 11).
   - Per-specimen 100/200/300% modulus is the stress at that strain, interpolated
     from each slot's stress_strain.csv.
   - The overlay chart (public/assets/img/rubber-testing/neo-stress-strain-overlay.webp)
     is drawn from the same 10 slot series, not the export's stress_strain.png,
     which has a hover tooltip baked in.
   - The motor log (xmotor.csv) gives a constant ~501.7 mm/min pull on every slot.
   - The video is Neoprene_v5_10_samples.mp4, specimen 01 (slot 2). Its first ~21 s are
     loading and gripping with the crosshead stationary, so video time = test
     time + 20.6. Retime syncOffset / speedKeyframes / phases when the video is
     synced exactly. */
